br.br:
1. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method of updating a patient record in a medical database, the method comprising, with a processor arrangement of an electronic device:receiving an image depicting a display screen of a patient monitoring system, wherein the image depicting the display screen of the patient monitor contains a depiction of displaying at least one vital signs data value of said patient;
evaluating at least one region of interest of said image comprising one of said vital signs data values to extract said one vital signs data value from said image;
updating the patient record with the extracted at least one vital signs data value; and
storing the image in a database such that the image is associated with the updated patient record.
2. (Original) The computer-implemented method of claim 1, further comprising generating an indicator value of an actual physical state of said patient from the extracted at least one vital signs data value and updating the patient record with the generated indicator value.
3. (Currently Amended) The computer-implemented method of claim 1, wherein the database; wherein the image is stored; is the medical database.
4. (Original) The computer-implemented method of claim 1, further comprising:
displaying the extracted at least one vital signs data value on a display device to a user;
receiving a verification command from said user; and
updating the patient record with the extracted at least one vital signs data value and storing the image in the medical database and/or the database in response to the received verification command.
5. (Original) The computer-implemented method of claim 1, wherein evaluating said image to extract the at least one vital signs data value from a region of interest in said image comprises:
identifying a region of interest comprising a vital signs data value in said image;
extracting the vital signs data value from the identified region of interest;
matching the extracted vital signs data value to a particular vital sign of the patient by comparing said vital signs data value against a library of expectation values of data values for different vital signs; and
updating a vital signs record of a vital sign in the patient record matched to the extracted vital signs data value with said extracted vital signs data value.
6. (Original) The computer-implemented method of claim 1, wherein said image is at least one photographic image or a screen capture.
7. The computer-implemented method of claim 1, further comprising receiving identification information of a person responsible for generating said image and associating at least one of the stored at least one vital signs data value and the stored image with the received identification information.
8-12. (Cancelled)911
13. (Currently Amended) A computer program product comprising anon-transitory computer readable storage medium having storing computer readable program instructions embodied therewith for that, when executed on a processor arrangement of an electronic deviceby one or more processors, cause the one or more processorsarrangement to implement the method of claim 1to:
receive an image depicting a display screen of a patient monitoring svstem, wherein the image depicting the display screen of the patient monitor contains a depiction of displaying at least one vital signs data value of said patient;
evaluate at least one region of interest of said image comprising one of said vital signs data values to extract said one vital signs data value from said image;
update the patient record with the extracted at least one vital signs data value; and
store the image in a database such that the image is associated with the updated patient record.
14. (Canceled)
15. (Currently Amended) An A system for updating a patient record in a medical database,
the system comprising:one or more processors;
a camera communicatively coupled to the one or more processors:
a display screen communicatively coupled to the one or more processors;
a data storage comprising a mask configured to align with a region of interest of a display screen of a patient monitoring system: and a memory communicatively coupled to the one or more processors, the memory comprising instructions for:
electronic client device comprising a processor arrangement, a camera communicatively coupled to said processor arrangement, a display screen communicatively coupled to said processor arrangement and a data storage device for storing a mask for aligning with a region of interest of a display screen of a patient monitoring system, wherein the processor arrangement is adapted to execute the method of claim 1receiving an image depicting the display screen of the patient monitoring system,
wherein the image depicting the display screen of the patient monitor contains a depiction of displaying at least one vital signs data value of said patient:
extracting a vital signs data value from the received image by evaluating at least one region of interest of the received image by applying the mask from the data storage, the at least one region of interest comprising the vital signs data value;
updating the patient record with the extracted at least one vital signs data value: and storing the image in a database such that the image is associated with the updated patient record.
